alue 1 in the no-memory fixture / 2 only when durable context is observed. There is still no held-out evidence that durable memory improves task outcomes, no measured retrieval SLO or end-to-end latency distribution, and durable-memory freshness remains unknown where source fingerprints are unavailable. Hosted checks, installed acceptance, independent review, and a fresh full run whose outer command exits zero remain outstanding. No inference provider was modified, and no push, PR, merge, or tag was performed.\n+\n+### Validation update — 2026-11-24, current rebased release snapshot\n+\n+On implementation head `52b54573264a1ac563119a9f318e57affc3a2753`, based on `release/v1.3.0` at `d03e6199f37bd024f17a807f00ed261291f8a02c`, `make build` passed in an isolated snapshot. The subsequent exact-head `make test` completed its Rust and terminal-security stages but failed in the second CLI shard. Rust core passed 53/53, Rust TUI passed 406/406, and the other Rust integration groups passed (1/1, 3/3, 4/4, and 1/1); the first CLI shard reported 3,108/3,112 passed with 4 skipped. The second CLI shard reported 3,057 tests: 3,043 passed, 1 failed, and 13 skipped. Its sole failure was `test/turn_semantics.test.ts`, “the same trajectory with a passing verifier is VERIFIED only through the verifier run”: expected `execution === COMPLETED`, received `FAILED`. Terminal scope fixtures passed and all lifecycle security gates printed success, but `make test` ended with `make: *** [Makefile:67: test] Error 1`; this is a failed aggregate run.\n+\n+The complete `turn_semantics.test.ts` file was then run alone on the same snapshot with an isolated HOME and passed 37/37 in 94.2 seconds. This non-reproduction does not erase the full-suite failure or establish its cause. The exact full-run log is `/tmp/context-maturity-make-test-52b54573-built.log`. No source was changed during these runs. The release branch has since advanced beyond this tested base; the implementation must be rebased and requalified at its current tip before making a release-level claim. Hosted checks, installed acceptance, independent review, and a clean exact-current full-suite run remain outstanding. No live inference was used and no inference provider, PR, release tag, or remote branch was changed.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a20bb2-48c0-7db0-bfc5-137d3a66f0eb","create_time":1795492678.4912531}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":46764,"sampled_through_sequence":46761,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
